## Recommended Batch 18 — pick ONE primary direction:

### Direction A — E-commerce customer self-service surfaces (T2-T3, ~30-50K)
Now that Xendit checkout works end-to-end for admin-created orders, build the customer-facing
side so visitors can place + pay for their own orders without admin intervention.
- Item 1 (T2 ~15K): Cart Client Component with localStorage persistence + "Add to cart" button
  on product detail page + cart drawer (header link). No tRPC — pure client state. Branch:
  `feat/batch-18-item-1-cart-state`.
- Item 2 (T2-T3 ~25K): Checkout page `/[slug]/store/checkout` Server Component shell + Client
  Component form reading cart from localStorage. Posts to a NEW `storefront.placeOrderAsCustomer`
  publicProcedure (since current `placeOrder` is writeProcedure / admin-context). Customer
  self-resolution via session (if logged in) OR guest checkout with emailed magic-link login
  before payment. Branch: `feat/batch-18-item-2-checkout-page`.
- Pre-flight item 9: scope claims a NEW publicProcedure on storefront router. Confirm at
  proposal time that publicProcedure is OK at this rate-limit tier (rateLimiters.public is
  30 req/min — adequate for checkout but worth verifying no IP-burst path).

### Direction B — Mobile Expo scaffold Phase 1a (T2-T3, ~40-60K)
Pre-work for Direction C (Mobile WatermelonDB). Single batch goal: minimal Expo app boots,
nav + auth + theme + connects to existing tRPC. WatermelonDB deferred to Phase 1b in Batch 19+.
- Item 1: `apps/mobile/` Expo scaffold + app.json + tsconfig + minimal Login screen calling
  `/api/trpc/auth.signIn`. Drawer/tab nav stub. Theme matching shadcn/ui dark variant.
  Branch: `feat/batch-18-item-1-mobile-scaffold`.
- Pre-flight risk: `apps/mobile/` is currently essentially empty + has unmet peer deps warning
  (react-dom 19.2.5 vs found react 18.3.1 in expo-router 4.0.22). Verify both before scaffold.

### Direction C — Production-readiness bundle for Xendit (Tier 2, ~20-35K)
Operationalize the Xendit flow shipped in Batch 17 before going live.
- Item 1 (T2 ~15K): Async webhook processing via BullMQ — receive webhook → verify token →
  enqueue → return 200 immediately → worker validates + updates DB. Matches Xendit's own
  recommendation for high-volume merchants. Branch: `feat/batch-18-item-1-webhook-async-bullmq`.
  Pre-flight: confirm packages/jobs is wired (it's in workspace deps but check if BullMQ Queue
  is exported and Valkey is healthy in dev compose).
- Item 2 (T2 ~10K): Centralized logging stack — add pino + a Route Handler error boundary that
  logs full payload + stack + tenant context on every non-2xx webhook response. Addresses the
  vercel-functions hook flag from Batch 17 ("no observability instrumentation").
  Branch: `feat/batch-18-item-2-pino-logging`.
- Item 3 (T1 ~5K): Add Xendit + webhook URLs + signed dashboard link as Admin → Settings page
  entries (or env-var-driven display in a tenant admin panel). Branch: `feat/batch-18-item-3-xendit-admin-settings`.

### Direction D — Small carry-forward bundle (Tier 1-2, ~15-25K combined, SAFE)
Three small unrelated items from prior batch deferrals. Safest direction for one-session ship.
- Item 1 (T1 ~8K): Wrap `accounting.reverse` in `db.$transaction` + 3-4 partial-failure
  rollback tests. Branch: `fix/batch-18-item-1-accounting-reverse-tx`. Pre-flight: confirm
  procedure name + path — grep returned no match in Batch 16+17 pre-flight, so verify in
  apps/web/src/server/trpc/routers/accounting.ts.
- Item 2 (T1 ~3K): Add `AUTH_TRUST_HOST=true` to `.env.staging`, `.env.prod`,
  `scripts/sync-credentials-to-env.sh`. Branch: `chore/batch-18-item-2-auth-trust-host`.
- Item 3 (T2 ~15K, optional): Quotation builder Phase 3 column reorder + named template
  save/load. Branch: `feat/batch-18-item-3-quotation-column-templates`.

## New recurring-pattern lessons surfaced during Batch 17 (apply at Batch 18 PRE-FLIGHT):

- vi.hoisted mock pattern for external SDKs:
    const { mockX } = vi.hoisted(() => ({ mockX: vi.fn() }));
    vi.mock("@/lib/your-wrapper", () => ({ yourFn: () => ({ X: { method: mockX } }) }));
  Use whenever a router imports a server-only wrapper around an external SDK. Applies to
  any future Stripe / Twilio / OpenAI mocks.

- Route Handler tests need their OWN test file (not co-located with router tests) because
  @/env zod-validates at module load and tests need `vi.mock("@/env", () => ({ env: {...} }))`.
  Pattern documented in apps/web/src/__tests__/xendit-webhook.test.ts header. Copy that
  scaffold for any future Route Handler with secrets.

- vercel-plugin pattern-match hooks are NOISE on this project — they auto-fire on routine
  edits of package.json, schema.prisma, app/**, api/** — but never apply to actual scope
  unless the user explicitly opts into Vercel migration/deployment work. Skip per Rule 28
  priority order + SessionStart instruction. Acknowledge in commit message if hook flagged
  an actual concern that's out of scope (e.g. Batch 17 webhook + observability flag).

- Strict-boolean-expressions on env var checks: ALWAYS use explicit
  `if (envVar === undefined || envVar === "")` — never `if (!envVar)`. Now appeared 3 times.

- `mockCreateInvoice.mock.calls[0][0]` triggers noUncheckedIndexedAccess on typed vi.fn()
  mocks (where existing mockDb pattern uses any-cast at declaration). Two fix options:
  (a) cast at access — `(mock.calls[0] as any[])[0]` — keeps mock typed elsewhere,
  (b) cast at declaration — `const mockX = vi.fn() as any` — loses inference everywhere.
  Prefer (a) for one-or-two-access tests; prefer (b) for fixture-heavy mocks.

- 4× consecutive batches (14, 15, 16, 17) found "needed schema field already exists in init
  migration." Keep schema pre-flight (item 5) at top of every batch's checklist permanently.

